  "description": "HEKDUZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H88 Dy8 N34 O39 4+,4(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.560-5.025 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.79-168.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(μ4-O)(μ3-OH)8(vht)4(NO3)2(H2O)8](NO3)4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
